From: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: pulse USXGMII SerDes block reset in full reset

Cable hotplug can leave the RTL8261BE host-side USXGMII AN engine stuck:
copper negotiates while the AN7581 PCS receives no partner word
(AN_STATS_0 stays zero) and the netdev carrier never comes up.  The
vendor 0x145 reset + patch-table reload + SDS reconfiguration in
rtl826x_rtk_serdes_full_reset() does not pulse the SerDes block itself.

The generic driver's link-up SDS reset (SDS page 0x20/0x02, assert
0x40 -> release 0xc0) is a no-op in this failure mode because the
PHY-side SerDes link bit is already set; only the netdev-carrier-down
path taken by 744/746 triggers at the right time.  Pulse the SerDes
block reset there as well, giving the stuck host AN engine a clean
DTE-XS restart before the retry loop re-arms.

Note: no TXPLL reset is performed - no reliable register sequence for
the RTL8261 TXPLL reset is available, and the generic driver's own SDS
reset does not touch the PLL either.

Signed-off-by: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -2700,11 +2700,28 @@ static int rtl826x_rtk_serdes_full_reset(struct phy_device *phydev)
 	ret = rtl826x_config_serdes_polarity(phydev);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;

+	/*
+	 * Pulse the USXGMII SerDes block reset (assert 0x40 -> release
+	 * 0xc0 on SDS page 0x20/reg 0x02), the same DTE-XS reset the
+	 * generic driver performs on link up.  In this failure mode the
+	 * PHY-side SerDes link bit is already up so the generic link-up
+	 * path never fires; only the netdev-carrier-down recovery that
+	 * reached us triggers at the right moment.
+	 */
+	ret = rtl826x_phy_patch_sds_set(phydev, 0x20, 0x02, 0x40);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+	msleep(20);
+	ret = rtl826x_phy_patch_sds_set(phydev, 0x20, 0x02, 0xc0);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+	msleep(100);
+
 	priv->rtk_serdes_pulse_count = 0;
 	priv->rtk_serdes_carrier_polls = 0;
 	priv->rtk_serdes_full_resets++;
 	priv->rtk_serdes_state = RTL826X_RTK_SERDES_PULSE;

 	return 0;
 }
--
2.43.0
